      "id": "data-sf-gov/open-data/rows",
      "provider": "data-sf-gov",
      "capability": "open-data/rows",
      "name": "Rows",
      "description": "Any question that needs actual records from a DataSF dataset. Get the 4x4 id from `datasets` and the column field names from `dataset` first. Use `row_count` to size a query before paging.",
      "creditsCost": 5,
      "perRecord": false,
      "options": [
        {
          "name": "cursor",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "Row offset to start from: the `next_cursor` of the previous page. Pattern: ^[0-9]{1,12}$."
        },
        {
          "name": "dataset_id",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "4x4 id (for example `3i4a-hu95`) or a data.sf.gov / data.sfgov.org URL containing it.",
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "name": "filters",
          "type": "object",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "Bare equality filters sent as `field=value` query parameters (for example {\"blklot\": \"3720009\"}); keys must be column field names, values strings."
        },
        {
          "name": "group",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "SoQL $group; pair with aggregates in `select`."
        },
        {
          "name": "limit",
          "type": "number",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "Rows per page. The portal caps a request at 50000; wide datasets with geometry should use far less.",
          "default": 100,
          "min": 1,
          "max": 50000
        },
        {
          "name": "order",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "SoQL $order, for example `filed_date DESC` or `count(*) DESC`. Default `:id` when no `group` is given."
        },
        {
          "name": "q",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "SoQL $q full-text search across all text columns."
        },
        {
          "name": "select",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "SoQL $select, for example `zoning_sim,districtna` or `zoning_sim,count(*)`. Default: all columns."
        },
        {
          "name": "where",
          "type": "string",
          "in": "body",
          "about": "SoQL $where, for example `zoning_sim like 'RH-1%'`, `filed_date between '2026-09-01T00:00:00' and '2026-09-02T00:00:00'`, `intersects(the_geom,'POINT(-122.3966 37.7897)')`, `within_circle(point,37.7897,-122.3966,50)`."
        }
      ],
      "response": {
        "about": "Query rows of any DataSF dataset through the SODA 2.1 endpoint https://data.sf.gov/resource/<4x4>.json with SoQL: `select` (columns, aggregates such as count(*)), `where` (SoQL predicates incl. like, between, intersects(the_geom,'POINT(lon lat)'), within_circle(point, lat, lon, meters), within_box), `order`, `group`, `q` (full text) and `filters` (bare field=value equality parameters), paged with `limit` (1-50000, default 100) and `cursor` (row offset). Without `order` (and without `group`) the program orders by the row id `:id` so pages are stable. Rows come back exactly as published: numbers and dates are strings, geometry is GeoJSON; `columns` lists the returned field names and Socrata types from the X-SODA2-Fields/Types headers. An unknown dataset id is not_found; a SoQL error (unknown column, bad syntax) is invalid_input carrying the portal's message; an empty page is a successful result with count 0.",
